---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_vi4_240",
  "series": "Band VI 4 (1677 - 1690)",
  "seq": 240,
  "text": "[[934.10]] <b>197.  Definitiones: Terminus vel aliquid, nihil [August 1688 bis Januar 1689 (?)]</b>\n [[934.11]] <tab/>[August 1688 bis Januar 1689 (?)] </p>\n<p> [[934.15]] <b>Terminus</b> vel <b>Aliquid</b> <i>A</i>, quicquid cogitari potest (: quasi Ens :) etiamsi fortasse\n[[934.16]] non sit possibile, ut motus perpetuus mechanicus. </p>\n<p> [[934.17]] <b>Nihil</b> <i>non A et non B et non C</i>, et caetera; seu <i>non-Y</i> (: hinc <i>nihili nulla sunt</i>\n[[934.18]] <i>attributa</i>, sive praedicata :). </p>\n<p> [[934.19]] <i>Y</i> significare mihi solet aliquid indefinitum, ut hoc loco quodcunque sit, <i>A, vel B, vel\n[[934.20]] C</i>; eodem modo sumo literam <i>X</i> aliamve ex posterioribus (: ut in Algebra speciosa :), est\n[[934.21]] igitur <i>Y</i> <b>Terminus indefinitus</b>. </p>\n<p> [[935.1]] <b>Valor Termini</b>, ut <i>A</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>B</i> · · <i>C</i>, quando scilicet declaramus, nos per <i>A</i> intelligere\n[[935.2]] <i>B</i> · · <i>C</i>, et loco <i>B</i> · · <i>C</i> per compendium ponere <i>A</i>; dicitur etiam terminus, <b>definitum</b>,\n[[935.3]] et valor ejus, <b>definitio.</b> </p>\n<p> [[935.4]] (: <i>B</i> · · <i>C</i> significat <i>B</i> et <i>C</i> ingredi valorem ipsius <i>A</i>, etsi non hoc loco designamus\n[[935.5]] quomodo, fieri enim potest ut similariter ingrediantur, ut <i>ignis</i> est <i>calidum lucidum</i>; sed\n[[935.6]] possunt tamen et dissimilariter connecti, ut <i>justitia</i> est <i>caritas sapientis</i>. Idem intellige si\n[[935.7]] plures termini ad valorem unius concurrant. :) </p>\n<p> [[935.8]] <b>Resolutio</b> seu <b>explicatio</b> est, si pro terminis ponantur valores. <b>Synthesis</b> si\n[[935.9]] contra. </p>\n<p> [[935.10]] <b>Continuata resolutio</b> est, si pro termino ponatur valor, et pro terminis valorem\n[[935.11]] ingredientibus rursus eorum valores; et ita porro (: quantum licet aut necesse est, nam si\n[[935.12]] perveniatur ad terminos irresolubiles, ibi quiescendum est, nec amplius progredi licet; si\n[[935.13]] resolutio talis sit, ut appareat lex progressionis, non amplius necesse est :). </p>\n<p> [[935.14]] Terminus <i>B</i> in termino <i>A</i> <b>involvi</b> dicitur si continuata explicatione hujus <i>A</i> ponitur\n[[935.15]] valor illius <i>B</i> (: ita ut certo explicandi modo effici possit prodire ipsummet <i>B</i> cum utique\n[[935.16]] ipse pro suo valore substitui possit :). </p>\n<p> [[935.17]] <i>Non ^#6+non A^#6-</i> idem est quod <i>A</i> (: et ideo <i>non non ^#6+non A</i>^#6- est ^#6+<i>non A</i>^#6- :). </p>\n<p> [[935.18]] Contradictio est <i>A non-A</i>. </p>\n<p> [[935.19]] <b>Non-Ens</b> seu <b>Impossibile</b> <b>est quod involvit contradictionem</b>, ut\n[[935.20]] <i>A</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>B</i> · · ^#4+<i>C ^#4-^#5+non-C</i>^#5-. </p>\n<p> [[935.21]] (: Hinc quod impossibile involvit, ipsummet impossibile est, nam quod involvit\n[[935.22]] involvens involvit involutum, itaque quod impossibile involvit contradictionem ipsi\n[[935.23]] involutam involvit. Hinc porro sequitur posita possibilitate involventis sequi vel\n[[936.1]] demonstratam esse possibilitatem involuti. Unde postremo videtur inferri posse posita\n[[936.2]] existentia involventis sequi existentiam involuti, etsi non simultaneam. :) </p>\n<p> [[936.3]] <b>Ens</b> seu <b>possibile</b> est non-impossibile seu <i>non ^#1+X · · ^#1-^#2+Y ^#2-^#3+non Y^#3-</i>. </p>\n<p> [[936.4]] <b>Necessarium</b> est cujus contradictorium est impossibile seu, si <i>non-A</i> est impossibile,\n[[936.5]] <i>A</i> est necessarium. </p>\n<p> [[936.6]] (: Verbi gratia <i>circulus non capacissimus isoperimetrorum</i> est Ens impossibile, ergo\n[[936.7]] <greek>tò</greek>: <i>non-^#4+circulus non ^#4-^#5+capacissimus isoperimetrorum</i>^#5- est ens necessarium, adeoque semper\n[[936.8]] existens, nam alterutrum dicit, vel non existere circulum, vel si existat, esse isoperimetrorum\n[[936.9]] capacissimum. :) </p>\n<p> [[936.10]] (: Dubium etiam hic nascitur, quod tale Ens necessarium impossibile sua definitione\n[[936.11]] involvit, ergo ipsum foret impossibile. Itaque addendum est <i>involvere</i> hic intelligi non\n[[936.12]] negative sed positive ac proinde diximus <b>poni</b> valorem ejus quod involvitur. :) </p>\n<p> [[936.13]] (: Sumo hic <i>Ens</i> generaliter pro omni objecto notionis possibilis, ergo et negativae. :) </p>\n<p> [[936.14]] <b>Contingens</b> est non-necessarium. </p>\n<p> [[936.15]] (: <b>Simplicius</b> est cujus possibilitas facilius demonstratur seu cujus synthesis est\n[[936.16]] brevior. :) </p>\n<p> [[936.17]] (: (: <b>Prius Natura</b> est (: involutum <Fn><i>Darüber</i>: ingrediens</Fn> simplicius :) <i>A</i> ipso <i>B</i> si demonstratio possibilitatis\n[[936.18]] ipsius <i>B</i> ita fieri potest assumta demonstratione possibilitatis ipsius <i>A</i>, ut nihil\n[[936.19]] assumatur inutile (: quod resolutione facta omitti potuisse appareat :). (: Itaque\n[[936.20]] demonstratio possibilitatis ipsius <i>A</i> lemma est serviens ad possibilitatem ipsius <i>B</i>\n[[936.21]] demonstrandam, neque ita quicquam mutatur demonstratio possibilitatis ipsius <i>B</i> nisi\n[[936.22]] quod pro valore ipsius <i>A</i> ponitur <i>A</i>. :) Dubito an haec duo coincidant <i>esse involutum\n[[936.23]] simplicius</i> et <i>inservire ad explicandum sine ambagibus</i>. [:) :)] </p>\n",
  "number": "197.",
  "title": "Definitiones: Terminus vel aliquid, nihil",
  "date": "[August 1688 bis Januar 1689 (?)]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:197. Definitiones: Terminus vel aliquid, nihil [August 1688 bis Januar 1689 (?)] [August 1688 bis Januar 1689 (?)] Terminus vel Aliquid A, quicquid cogitari potest (: quasi Ens :) etiamsi fortasse non sit possibile, ut motus perpetuus mechanicus. Nihil non A et non B et non C, et caetera; seu non-Y ...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>